NEMESIS / OPERATOR — LIGHTWEIGHT FIRST START

Map: https://globe.airplanes.live/
KDE Plasma Wayland session; live wallpaper launches from XDG autostart.
Offline map is only a static status indicator, never cached aircraft data.

Included by default: a full usable desktop, Firefox, Konsole, Dolphin,
RTL-SDR and Airspy hardware utilities, a basic ADS-B decoder, safe local
diagnostics, WireGuard client and signed Arch package management.
No automatic RF capture, scanning, VPN or SSH remote service.

Optional toolkits (text manifests ship in live image, not the packages):
  nemesis-kit list            List curated toolkits
  nemesis-kit show aviation   Preview ADS-B/ISM extras
  nemesis-kit show airspy     Preview Soapy Airspy backend
  nemesis-kit show gnss       Preview GNSS tools
  nemesis-kit show network    Preview advanced network diagnostics
  nemesis-kit show rf-lab     Preview heavyweight Gqrx/GNU Radio
  nemesis-kit show development
  nemesis-kit show gis

After an installer with proper administrator authentication is validated,
the installed-system administrator may select and install only what is
needed with 'nemesis-kit install KIT'. This refuses installation on the
ephemeral live ISO, does not bypass signatures or invoke sudo, and makes
no system change merely by listing or showing tools.

Live-only operator login has a locked password and no sudo access; it
is not an installer or persistent workstation security policy. Do not
replicate auto-login or disable screen locking on an installed system.

Wallpaper source: https://github.com/pskeffington/linux_live_wallpaper
Third-party map: https://globe.airplanes.live/ (not redistributed).
